{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only observed data variable scored by a sampling statement is the top-level data variable `y`, and it is observed exactly once with the built-in distribution `normal`. The context inputs `M`, `N`, `x0`, and `X` are not protected; they are used only as sizes, baselines, and predictors. All parameters have built-in prior sampling statements before their later use, and the model does not use forbidden direct log-density manipulation.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> M; // Number of covariates
  int<lower=0> N; // Number of observations

  vector[M] x0;   // Covariate baselines
  matrix[N, M] X; // Covariate design matrix

  array[N] real y;      // Variates
}

transformed data {
  matrix[N, M] deltaX;
  for (n in 1:N) {
    deltaX[n,] = X[n] - x0';
  }
}

parameters {
  real alpha;          // Intercept
  vector[M] beta;      // Slopes
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement Variability
}

model {
  // Prior model
  alpha ~ normal(25, 5);
  beta ~ normal(0, 3);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 5);

  // Vectorized observation model
  y ~ normal(alpha + deltaX * beta, sigma);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  vector[N] mu = alpha + deltaX * beta;
  array[N] real y_pred = normal_rng(alpha + deltaX * beta, sigma);
}
